sdcl - a service definition configuration language
--------------------------------------------------

 sdcl is a text file format that abstracts service definitions
for various service managers such as OpenRC, s6-rc, or systemd.
The sdcl package provides tools to convert files from the sdcl
format to the native formats of all supported service managers.

 The goal is to provide a unified format for service definition,
in order for distributions to be able to offer a choice of
service managers without extra packaging or maintenance work.

 See https://skarnet.org/software/sdcl/ for details.


* Installation
  ------------

 See the INSTALL file.


